## Why This Is Asked
New angle on CBA: gating cross‑app features via an on‑device policy engine, balancing UX, energy, and safety with cloud updates.

## Key Concepts
- On‑device policy engines and gating rules
- Resource awareness (battery, thermal, memory)
- Telemetry footprint and privacy compliance
- Rollout strategy and break‑even analysis

## Code Example
```javascript
function shouldRunFeature(state, policy) {
  if (state.battery < 20) return false;
  if (state.temperature > 45) return false;
  if (state.freeMemory < 200) return false;
  return policy.allowsFeature;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you quantify risk of safety incidents vs false positives?
- What metrics would drive policy update cadence and rollouts across device generations?

## Why This Is Asked
This question tests the ability to model costs for on-device features with privacy constraints, focusing on storage, compute, telemetry, and go/no-go criteria. It emphasizes practical trade-offs and measurable outcomes.

## Key Concepts
- On-device compute budgeting
- Data minimization and privacy compliance
- Telemetry design and cost optimization
- Index sizing and update cadence
- Break-even analysis and milestone-driven go/no-go criteria

## Code Example
```javascript
function computeCBA(params) {
  const storageCost = params.indexMB * 0.15;
  const energyCost = params.annualWh * 0.0003;
  const telemetryCost = params.dailyTelemetryKB * 365 * 0.00001;
  const privacyAuditCost = params.userCount * 0.10;

  return {
    storageCost,
    energyCost,
    telemetryCost,
    privacyAuditCost,
    totalYear1Cost: storageCost + energyCost + telemetryCost + privacyAuditCost
  };
}
```

## Why This Is Asked

Tests ability to translate a feature into a concrete CBA with privacy constraints, rollout strategy, and measurable ROI.

## Key Concepts

- On-device perceptual hashing
- Memory and CPU budgeting for fingerprint indices
- Data savings vs latency trade-offs
- Privacy/compliance, consent flows
- Rollout plans, offline fallback, drift maintenance, ROI calculation

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo: fingerprint a media item and decide upload
function shouldUpload(media) {
  const fp = perceptualFingerprint(media);
  const exists = fingerprintIndex.has(fp);
  if (exists) return false;
  fingerprintIndex.add(fp);
  return true;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you measure and validate data savings at scale?
- How handle hash collisions and index eviction?
- What telemetry would you collect for ROI without compromising privacy?

## Why This Is Asked
Assess ability to quantify economics of on-device ML features, balancing privacy, latency, and cloud savings at scale across enterprises.

## Key Concepts
- On-device indexing and embeddings
- Energy budgets and edge compute
- Delta-sync and privacy-compliant telemetry
- Multi-tenant rollout and org-level scaling
- Regulatory/compliance costs and go/no-go criteria

## Code Example
```javascript
// Simple relevant cash-flow function for CBA
function cbaNPV(cf, r) {
  let npv = 0;
  for (let t = 0; t < cf.length; t++) {
    npv += cf[t] / Math.pow(1 + r, t + 1);
  }
  return npv;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you validate the energy model across devices with different hardware?
- How would you quantify productivity uplift from improved search latency in organizations?

